  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "summary": "(checkbox 1; SUPERSEDES 01-R1's flat ten-key input map): `blueprint.input` is EXACTLY five mappings named `button_1`..`button_5` — one collapsible section per button. Each section mapping carries EXACTLY the keys `name` "
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "summary": "(checkbox 2; carries 01-R2): each section's nested input map carries EXACTLY five inputs: `button_N_entity` — a REQUIRED event-entity input (entity selector restricted to `domain: event`, NO `default` key) — plus four ac"
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "summary": "(carried 01-R3): the blueprint loads in Home Assistant (Settings -> Automations -> Blueprints) with no import error."
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "summary": "(checkbox 3; SUPERSEDES 01-R4 push-only dispatch and 01-R5 non-pushed-runs-nothing): the automation dispatches each of the four event types — `pushed`, `held`, `doubleTapped`, `released` — on each button N to that button"
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "summary": "(checkbox 4): the automation root carries `mode: parallel`, so two overlapping button presses (or a held-then-released pair) both run instead of aborting each other (runtime leg U1; the structural leg is the exact mode v"
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "summary": "(checkbox 5): HA's blueprint default configuration view shows ONLY the five collapsed section headers (\"Button 1\"..\"Button 5\" with their numbered icons), not ~20-25 loose fields (UI leg U1; the structural legs are R1's `"
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "summary": "(carried 01-R7): the leading header comment documents the four supported event types and the MQTT/Hubitat origin of the event-entity pattern, per CONTEXT.md (01-D2 rule unchanged: provenance prose lives only in the heade"
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "summary": "(checkbox 6; carries 01-R8 revised): generic by design — only the button NUMBERING and the numbered `mdi` icons are fixed UI; no vendor, model, node id, room name, or concrete entity id is baked in anywhere (configuratio"
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "summary": "(checkbox 7; carries 01-R6): `python3 scripts/validate_blueprint.py blueprints/automation/generic_scene_controller.yaml` still exits 0 (on the restructured file), is still documented verbatim in README, and the unittest "
    },
    {
      "id": "R10",
      "summary": "(scope fence; revised 01-R9): everything from tickets 03-09 stays OUT: no `multiple: true` entity selectors (03), no central `variables:` (03), no `not_from: [unavailable, unknown]` restart guard (04), no smart toggle/cy"
    }
